cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it and the paper it accompanies once published."
title: "DAIM-OS Packet-In Artifact: Reconstructing the DAIM-OS Table-and-Signal Control Path"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Banjar
    given-names: Ameen
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0871-5153"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-08
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ameen-banjar/daim-os-packetin-artifact"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility artifact for "Reconstructing the DAIM-OS Table-and-Signal
  Control Path: An Executable OpenFlow 1.3 Artifact and Evaluation." Contains
  a mutex-protected C core implementing five writable DAIM-OS tables, a
  switch-adapter boundary to Open vSwitch, a real Os-Ken OpenFlow 1.3
  controller bridged to the core via ctypes, and a matched adapter-overhead
  microbenchmark with raw data, stage-decomposed reactive-path measurements,
  sustained-load profiling, cross-environment checks, and readable regenerated
  figures with reproducible analysis scripts.
keywords:
  - software-defined networking
  - OpenFlow
  - Open vSwitch
  - DAIM-OS
  - reproducible systems research
references:
  - type: software
    title: "DAIM-OS: Distributed Active Information Model Operating System Specification"
